[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-160888"] :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨z+y,\\,2y+z,\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=x-y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x-y)=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-y)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨z+y,\\,2y+z,\\,xy⟩{|}_{z=x-y} \\\\  & =⟨(x-y)+y,\\,2y+(x-y),\\,xy⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{{x}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{x+y}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{xy}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z+y,\\,2y+z,\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(x)\\cdot 1-(x+y)\\cdot (-1)+xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-x+x+y+xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y+xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(y+xy)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}x{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2x+{x}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(2(1)+{1}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-161446/selection/fe6c2cba43067fbe7d2575198bda50b41982d819e828e440aacaac114a8d72da" :answer/id #uuid "f2811914-6f70-56dd-841f-80b6402cbcf0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-Q$ and $∂z$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161446/selection/85627d5e7e09590fdc634d73a62928ace77f214e4f071d78b8242fe0cc1c2d52" :answer/id #uuid "5e51c96c-bd01-54a2-87bb-25a5adc42bef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $∂z$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161446/selection/856a1f32a48bf97280eb35c079afcb343680245367f9df8c8fb479958e752163" :answer/id #uuid "c3f83a6d-f3dd-5130-aa17-a33405289612" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $∂x$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161446/selection/65e3ff89b491f395c06de7a718e2d00584b8363bde74dc1f421f759b52437571" :answer/id #uuid "720e5c72-156a-529a-b954-0fadefeedcdc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-Q$ and $∂x$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161446/selection/3d15be89fa6663025bf1fbc07ca0271a6e2979209feb918c3f25bc75b55659af" :answer/id #uuid "b1158736-1de5-5fbf-b48d-af048d0836ef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-R$ and $∂z$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161446/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "295d3669-0b18-50cf-bcb3-1701ccc4eef7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161446/selection/fe6c2cba43067fbe7d2575198bda50b41982d819e828e440aacaac114a8d72da" :answer-field/choices ["q-161446/selection/fe6c2cba43067fbe7d2575198bda50b41982d819e828e440aacaac114a8d72da" "q-161446/selection/85627d5e7e09590fdc634d73a62928ace77f214e4f071d78b8242fe0cc1c2d52" "q-161446/selection/856a1f32a48bf97280eb35c079afcb343680245367f9df8c8fb479958e752163" "q-161446/selection/65e3ff89b491f395c06de7a718e2d00584b8363bde74dc1f421f759b52437571" "q-161446/selection/3d15be89fa6663025bf1fbc07ca0271a6e2979209feb918c3f25bc75b55659af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161446" :question/id #uuid "1b125418-463d-5d64-af0c-e0bb9a3a435d" :question/math-academy-id "q-161446" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $x=k(y,z)$ for $(y,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(P+\\frac{∂k}{∂y}-R\\frac{∂k}{})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $x=k(y,z),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(y,z)=⟨k(y,z),\\,y,\\,z⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂k}{∂z},\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂k}{∂y} & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{∂k}{∂z} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨1,\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂z}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂z}⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(P+(-Q\\,)\\frac{∂k}{∂y}-R\\frac{∂k}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161446/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55cd2fdb-4cae-5f0b-bea0-e845d51190e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161446"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161457/selection/e83b7199a7a0e2aa22a80ed4ecfb5cde148e07704adc4cb7622ad2c977cfad95" :answer/id #uuid "bf1d4e7b-209b-5203-be60-bd097c1f0b6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∂g,\\text{ }Q,\\text{ }∂y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161457/selection/70f3ed2f61065687b3dadd09142dd17814d767fb0778988db8bbd479dd12cce2" :answer/id #uuid "111d65f2-376d-5456-9f07-63ef6bd264a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∂g,\\text{ }-Q,\\text{ }∂Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161457/selection/970233da9fd2fbe63609692d03590c6ee31fe66a1c7892ba2ef6b9554e07a631" :answer/id #uuid "ef7c9ca4-c7a4-5650-bcd4-3bed3109a217" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∂g,\\text{ }-Q,\\text{ }∂y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161457/selection/7dbd4c35b90a891ca8ffb8ffc7827126a9fe5e10d2050757754098a58d83a410" :answer/id #uuid "79bee6ea-c2d0-5ebd-850e-e267dc95b68e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∂g,\\text{ }Q,\\text{ }∂z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161457/selection/963504c384925fae401c20325d6918283d9ede788226f350ccc71da4001251bc" :answer/id #uuid "ba6d0d49-fa17-573a-a761-cdf2234d23ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∂g,\\text{ }-Q,\\text{ }∂z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161457/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e0b1c14-ccfb-5db5-aa5d-3a11009350e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161457/selection/e83b7199a7a0e2aa22a80ed4ecfb5cde148e07704adc4cb7622ad2c977cfad95" :answer-field/choices ["q-161457/selection/e83b7199a7a0e2aa22a80ed4ecfb5cde148e07704adc4cb7622ad2c977cfad95" "q-161457/selection/70f3ed2f61065687b3dadd09142dd17814d767fb0778988db8bbd479dd12cce2" "q-161457/selection/970233da9fd2fbe63609692d03590c6ee31fe66a1c7892ba2ef6b9554e07a631" "q-161457/selection/7dbd4c35b90a891ca8ffb8ffc7827126a9fe5e10d2050757754098a58d83a410" "q-161457/selection/963504c384925fae401c20325d6918283d9ede788226f350ccc71da4001251bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161457" :question/id #uuid "417f7e3b-659c-5f7d-913c-decf384148f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161457" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{}{∂x}-\\frac{∂g}{}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $z=g(x,y),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,g(x,y)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂x}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\frac{∂g}{∂x} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\end{aligned}|=⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161457/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55cd2fdb-4cae-5f0b-bea0-e845d51190e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161457"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161536/selection/7b9fbdbadaf16c2e9a120b251a8e9ba025197e7cd9d600d1c76e59a282cb9130" :answer/id #uuid "6a3b960d-98aa-5d4e-b5e5-285f0f954734" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-1}-e}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161536/selection/b3d5394476291f0121976a01905525831ebf0664105185d0d1ad60cd90d1eb6f" :answer/id #uuid "fac6e977-a8fc-5b74-b3c2-17fafd400bae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3e+{e}^{-1}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161536/selection/a0ff91f510502bc53b224485fa0c923c77da083350113018652cb4ee08b55952" :answer/id #uuid "8f1c3dc7-6025-5c0e-a957-4902befc69a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3e-{e}^{-1}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161536/selection/02d6498459131c41ac38bb74c67672b2053b915ca1d576e02cc5b6a48178cd1c" :answer/id #uuid "b924de85-1175-5542-94c9-37664d8a7f51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5e+2{e}^{-1}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161536/selection/589b3e1fb62442446af90eb7c5d4952342eaec0709daaa1937ebc642971352f1" :answer/id #uuid "42d9d685-96da-5132-8f72-febac7e8127e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7e-{e}^{-1}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161536/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "056f196e-3bbc-50c0-89ba-8f81c9154689" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161536/selection/7b9fbdbadaf16c2e9a120b251a8e9ba025197e7cd9d600d1c76e59a282cb9130" :answer-field/choices ["q-161536/selection/7b9fbdbadaf16c2e9a120b251a8e9ba025197e7cd9d600d1c76e59a282cb9130" "q-161536/selection/b3d5394476291f0121976a01905525831ebf0664105185d0d1ad60cd90d1eb6f" "q-161536/selection/a0ff91f510502bc53b224485fa0c923c77da083350113018652cb4ee08b55952" "q-161536/selection/02d6498459131c41ac38bb74c67672b2053b915ca1d576e02cc5b6a48178cd1c" "q-161536/selection/589b3e1fb62442446af90eb7c5d4952342eaec0709daaa1937ebc642971352f1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161536" :question/id #uuid "1ba113f9-8e6f-5431-9993-fef9b213da77" :question/math-academy-id "q-161536" :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z={e}^{x}$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x})={e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x})=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩{|}_{z={e}^{x}} \\\\  & =⟨{{y}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{x+{e}^{x}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{0}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y\\cdot ({e}^{x})-(x+{e}^{x})\\cdot 0+0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-y{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[-\\frac{{y}^{2}{e}^{x}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{[{e}^{x}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-1}-e}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161536/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaa6b152-86d3-5f96-8a94-57f86a17a84d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161536"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-161553"] :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=-x-y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-x-y)=-1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-x-y)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩{|}_{z=-x-y} \\\\  & =⟨{{{e}^{x}}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{{e}^{y}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{1-x-y}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-({e}^{x})\\cdot (-1)-({e}^{y})\\cdot (-1)+1-x-y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({e}^{x}+{e}^{y}+1-x-y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}+{e}^{y}+1-x-y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{e}^{x}y+{e}^{y}+y-xy-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}+e+1-x-\\frac{1}{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}-x-\\frac{1}{2}+e)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{e}^{x}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{x}{2}+ex]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =e-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}+e-1 \\\\  & =2e-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
